Acts of Defamation
10. (a) For the purposes of this Act, if a false statement or false information is given through the following means or matters, it shall be deemed an act of defamation.

(1) By a conversation held, or by words spoken, or by information given;

(2) By a writing written or published, or by a drawing drawn, or by a photograph or image;

(3) By a drawing, photograph or image displayed, or by a sound played;

(4) By a writing, statement, photograph, song or any other information broadcast through radio, television or other similar means, or published through the internet;

