(d) For the purposes of subsection (a)(3) of this Article, the following principles shall apply in determining whether a statement made or information given is attributable to the defamed party.

(1) If the name or photograph of the defamed party has been used, that statement or information shall be deemed to be attributable to the defamed party;

(2) Even if the name or photograph of the defamed party has not been used, if it is reasonable to believe, from the manner in which words or information have been used in making the statement or giving the information, that it refers to the defamed party, that statement or information shall be deemed to be attributable to the defamed party;

(3) Even if it is stated that the statement made or the information given is directed at a party that does not exist, or even if it is stated that it concerns a party other than the defamed party, if it is reasonable

